WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:08.164
Make a balloon rocket. It travels along a string using escaping air, without flames or fuel.

00:08.964 --> 00:18.035
Gather one balloon, one straight straw, two to three metres of string, tape, measuring tape, and a stopwatch.

00:18.835 --> 00:25.063
First, pass the string through the straw. The straw acts as the moving guide.

00:25.863 --> 00:33.337
Tie the string securely between two stable supports. Pull it tight, and leave a clear path.

00:34.137 --> 00:42.448
Inflate the balloon and pinch its neck closed. Tape it to the straw, with the opening pointing backwards.

00:43.248 --> 00:50.682
At the starting mark, release the balloon neck. Air rushes back and the balloon slides forward.

00:51.482 --> 01:00.089
Measure the distance between two marks, and time the journey. Divide distance by time to estimate average speed.

01:00.889 --> 01:09.088
Repeat three times. Change one thing at a time, such as balloon inflation, and compare results.

01:09.888 --> 01:18.521
Keep the path clear and never point the balloon at anyone. This demonstrates thrust; it is not a powered rocket.

